f  antioxidant rich veggies  plus some healthy fats in the seeds and  nuts  and i am low-key obsessed with halloumi  cheese and i don't think i've ever seen  a youtuber cook with it so brownie  points  to miranda for throwing that into the  mix but seriously this meal is  inherently  obviously very healthy and if we look at  the  different components you're really  talking about some of the most  nutrient-rich ingredients that money can  buy but when put together  it like looks and feels very much like a  chef worthy meal something that you  could easily get at like a really fancy  trendy restaurant  in la this is comfort food  without the side of diet culture and i  think that comfort food as a term  has often been co-opted by diet culture  to mean  bad foods but to me it can easily be  nutritious foods that just feel cozy and  comforting to the  soul that's what this meal feels like to  me  and as a result i think it's likely just  as emotionally satisfying  as it probably is physically satiating  all right so let's talk about miranda's  day starting with the stats  and a quick trigger warning here that i  am about to talk numbers  so if that's something that you want to  skip ahead for you do you  so according to my super crude  calculations we're looking at around  1800 calories  assuming she did have some of those  pancakes and she's getting around 27  of her calories from protein 30 from  carbs  and 43 from fat so this is by no means a  keto diet but it is still pretty low on  the carbs and high on the fat  she's also hitting pretty much all of  her micronutrients though she's  a little bit low on iron zinc and is at  the lower  range of healthy for fiber at 27 grams  now as for her antioxidants i actually  didn't even include the skin supplement  in my analysis since the website doesn't  even list anything  other than vitamin c but without it she  was coming in at over  300 of her vitamin c needs uh 1500 of  her vitamin a needs  and 200 of her vitamin e so  i think she's probably good on that  front  now while overdosing on vitamins isn't  usually a huge concern when it comes to  food  depending on what her supplements offer  in terms of vitamin a  and e she could be at risk of vitamin  toxicity so that is definitely something  to watch  we can get too much of a good thing  now there's obviously a lot to like here  as miranda's diet is  clearly nutrient dense and her meals  look  delicious colorful and fresh her intake  while possibly a little bit lower than  what i would have predicted for her  isn't the extreme deficits that we often  see here on  my channel and she doesn't seem to be  demonizing any particular foods  or food groups here so we got pancakes  you got cheese you got oil you know all  commonly shunned ingredients here in the  youtube wellness space so  i definitely appreciate that so i think  that all i would suggest  is to maybe just mix in a few more whole  grains so that's rich in iron  so she could switch up her smoothie and  do  some oatmeal sometimes maybe add quinoa  to a lunch salad  swap out the chicken sometimes for a  plant-based protein like soybeans or  lentils  also tahini tahini is a really great  source of iron so  she could easily add that you know a  little bit into her dressing or  put a spoonful into her smoothie as for  her relationship with food  um ultimately this one video doesn't  give me nearly enough information to  comment on the adequacy  of miranda's overall diet nor does it  really tell me a whole lot about her  food philosophy  or her relationship with food but i will  say that i appreciate  that i didn't hear a ton of explicit  diet culture language  or demonizing any particular foods or  food groups  the worst that we heard was a little bit  of misinformation about lemon water  but let's be real it wouldn't be a  victoria's secret what i in a day  without  some claim about drinking lemon water in  the morning  so i guess in the grand scheme of all of  these videos i've reviewed  that seems pretty benign so in  conclusion  a quick reminder to please be kind in  the comments  and that this video was in no way a  criticism of miranda herself  or really even her diet i'm hoping to  now use these videos as kind of  teachable moments to teach  gentle nutrition so hopefully you were  able to  take some of these useful tips and ideas  away on how to optimize your meals and  snacks  and on that note that is all from me  today thank you again to squarespace for  sponsoring this video  if you liked it be sure to give it the  thumbs up  leave me a comment below on who you'd  like to see me review next  subscribe to the channel and i'll see  you next time on abby's kitchen  bye  you
 

